Package: pprof
Type: Package
Title: Provider Profiling: Risk Adjustment, Standardized Measures, Hypothesis
    Tests and Reference Distributions
Version: 2.0.6
Date: 2026-11-07
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yubo", "Shao", email = "ybshao@umich.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kevin", "He", email = "kevinhe@umich.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Components for profiling health care providers, organised by
    analysis step rather than by quality measure: data preparation and
    checks, risk-adjustment models with high-dimensional provider effects
    (fixed, random and correlated random effects; logistic, linear and
    survival outcomes), direct and indirect standardized measures with their
    standard errors, hypothesis tests for provider effects (exact, score and
    Wald statistics with naive, patient-clustered robust and stabilized
    variances), covariate tests, confidence intervals, theoretical and
    size-stratified empirical null reference distributions, inter-unit
    reliability, penalized variable selection with unpenalized provider
    effects, and plots. Every quality measure is assembled from these
    components. Supersedes 'pprof' 1.0.3, 'pprofR' and 'grplasso'.
